    "description": "Write a Python function called `alternating_sum_1_while` that must calculate an alternating sum beginning with multiplier 1. Practice while loop syntax.\nDifficulty: Intermediate.\nExamples:\n  alternating_sum_1_while([1, 2, 3]) -> 2\n  alternating_sum_1_while([]) -> 0",
    "initialCode": "def alternating_sum_1_while(values):\n    pass",
    "solution": "# Example 1: canonical function approach\ndef alternating_sum_1_while(values):\n    index = 0\n    sign = 1\n    total = 0\n    while index < len(values):\n        total += sign * values[index]\n        sign *= -1\n        index += 1\n    return total\n\nprint(alternating_sum_1_while([1, 2, 3]))  # Expected: 2\nprint(alternating_sum_1_while([]))  # Expected: 0\n\n# Example 2: nested helper approach\ndef solve_problem_6138(values):\n    def calculate():\n        index = 0\n        sign = 1\n        total = 0\n        while index < len(values):\n            total += sign * values[index]\n            sign *= -1\n            index += 1\n        return total\n    return calculate()\n\nprint(solve_problem_6138([1, 2, 3]))\n\n# Example 3: static method approach\nclass Problem6138Solution:\n    @staticmethod\n    def alternating_sum_1_while(values):\n        index = 0\n        sign = 1\n        total = 0\n        while index < len(values):\n            total += sign * values[index]\n            sign *= -1\n            index += 1\n        return total\n\nprint(Problem6138Solution.alternating_sum_1_while([]))\n\n# Example 4: assigned result approach\nresult = alternating_sum_1_while([1, 2, 3])\nprint(result)\n\n# Example 5: direct call\nprint(alternating_sum_1_while([5, -1]))",
