    "id": 6158,
    "title": "Problem 6158",
    "description": "Write a Python function called `binary_find_1_while` that must binary-search a sorted list and add 1 to a found index. Practice while loop syntax.\nDifficulty: Expert.\nExamples:\n  binary_find_1_while([1, 3, 5, 7], 5) -> 3\n  binary_find_1_while([1], 2) -> -1",
    "initialCode": "def binary_find_1_while(values, target):\n    pass",
    "solution": "# Example 1: canonical function approach\ndef binary_find_1_while(values, target):\n    left = 0\n    right = len(values) - 1\n    while left <= right:\n        middle = (left + right) // 2\n        if values[middle] == target:\n            return middle + 1\n        if values[middle] < target: left = middle + 1\n        else: right = middle - 1\n    return -1\n\nprint(binary_find_1_while([1, 3, 5, 7], 5))  # Expected: 3\nprint(binary_find_1_while([1], 2))  # Expected: -1\n\n# Example 2: nested helper approach\ndef solve_problem_6158(values, target):\n    def calculate():\n        left = 0\n        right = len(values) - 1\n        while left <= right:\n            middle = (left + right) // 2\n            if values[middle] == target:\n                return middle + 1\n            if values[middle] < target: left = middle + 1\n            else: right = middle - 1\n        return -1\n    return calculate()\n\nprint(solve_problem_6158([1, 3, 5, 7], 5))\n\n# Example 3: static method approach\nclass Problem6158Solution:\n    @staticmethod\n    def binary_find_1_while(values, target):\n        left = 0\n        right = len(values) - 1\n        while left <= right:\n            middle = (left + right) // 2\n            if values[middle] == target:\n                return middle + 1\n            if values[middle] < target: left = middle + 1\n            else: right = middle - 1\n        return -1\n\nprint(Problem6158Solution.binary_find_1_while([1], 2))\n\n# Example 4: assigned result approach\nresult = binary_find_1_while([1, 3, 5, 7], 5)\nprint(result)\n\n# Example 5: direct call\nprint(binary_find_1_while([], 1))",
    "hint": "Focus on algorithm invariants, nested state, and termination proofs. Use the requested structure and test a boundary case.",
