    "description": "Write a Python function called `decode_runs_1_while` that must decode value-count pairs and append marker 1. Practice while loop syntax.\nDifficulty: Expert.\nExamples:\n  decode_runs_1_while([[\"a\", 2], [\"b\", 1]]) -> [\"a\", \"a\", \"b\", 1]\n  decode_runs_1_while([]) -> [1]",
    "initialCode": "def decode_runs_1_while(pairs):\n    pass",
    "solution": "# Example 1: canonical function approach\ndef decode_runs_1_while(pairs):\n    result = []\n    index = 0\n    while index < len(pairs):\n        value, count = pairs[index]\n        repeated = 0\n        while repeated < count:\n            result.append(value); repeated += 1\n        index += 1\n    result.append(1)\n    return result\n\nprint(decode_runs_1_while([[\"a\", 2], [\"b\", 1]]))  # Expected: [\"a\", \"a\", \"b\", 1]\nprint(decode_runs_1_while([]))  # Expected: [1]\n\n# Example 2: nested helper approach\ndef solve_problem_6173(pairs):\n    def calculate():\n        result = []\n        index = 0\n        while index < len(pairs):\n            value, count = pairs[index]\n            repeated = 0\n            while repeated < count:\n                result.append(value); repeated += 1\n            index += 1\n        result.append(1)\n        return result\n    return calculate()\n\nprint(solve_problem_6173([[\"a\", 2], [\"b\", 1]]))\n\n# Example 3: static method approach\nclass Problem6173Solution:\n    @staticmethod\n    def decode_runs_1_while(pairs):\n        result = []\n        index = 0\n        while index < len(pairs):\n            value, count = pairs[index]\n            repeated = 0\n            while repeated < count:\n                result.append(value); repeated += 1\n            index += 1\n        result.append(1)\n        return result\n\nprint(Problem6173Solution.decode_runs_1_while([]))\n\n# Example 4: assigned result approach\nresult = decode_runs_1_while([[\"a\", 2], [\"b\", 1]])\nprint(result)\n\n# Example 5: direct call\nprint(decode_runs_1_while([[9, 1]]))",
